WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.110 --> 00:06.111
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

3
00:06.194 --> 00:08.030
THERE IS NO RELATION TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

4
00:09.740 --> 00:10.741
[sighs]

5
00:10.824 --> 00:12.326
EPISODE 2

6
00:12.409 --> 00:13.410
[sighs]

7
00:15.287 --> 00:16.663
-[gasps] -[♪ regal music playing]

8
00:30.761 --> 00:31.762
[sighs]

9
00:39.227 --> 00:40.729
[popping]

10
00:46.985 --> 00:49.446
[♪ dramatic music playing]

11
00:52.240 --> 00:54.326
[shrieking]

12
00:59.498 --> 01:01.124
[♪ guitar music plays]

13
01:01.208 --> 01:02.209
[yells]

14
01:03.877 --> 01:05.295
No, no, no, no, no, no, no!

15
01:08.632 --> 01:10.217
[in Korean] Hey…

16
01:10.926 --> 01:12.427
You all right?

17
01:12.511 --> 01:14.429
-[screams, pants] -[groans]

18
01:15.097 --> 01:17.057
-[in English] What are you doing? -Man… [groans]

19
01:17.140 --> 01:19.267
[pants]

20
01:19.351 --> 01:20.727
[in Korean] Come on!

21
01:22.562 --> 01:23.647
[in English] Who are you?

22
01:24.356 --> 01:26.525
You ruined my farm, didn't you?

23
01:26.608 --> 01:30.529
[in Korean] Wait, what in the… What's she even saying?

24
01:31.405 --> 01:32.531
Hey, just wait.

25
01:33.198 --> 01:34.366
Okay.

26
01:36.326 --> 01:39.079
This land is my property. You fainted right in front of me,

27
01:39.162 --> 01:41.164
and that's why I had to lay you down for a bit.

28
01:41.248 --> 01:43.458
I mean, why are you acting like this? Huh?

29
01:44.126 --> 01:45.669
-[in English] What? -Oh.

30
01:46.711 --> 01:48.130
THIS LAND IS MY PROPERTY.

31
01:48.213 --> 01:49.840
YOU FAINTED, AND I LAID YOU DOWN FOR A BIT.

32
01:49.923 --> 01:51.091
WHY ARE YOU ACTING LIKE THIS?

33
01:51.716 --> 01:53.677
[scoffs, grunts]

34
01:54.219 --> 01:57.514
You're a scam artist. So stealing from my farm wasn't enough?

35
01:58.098 --> 01:59.099
[in Korean] Hey, what…

36
01:59.683 --> 02:00.684
Man, what is she saying?

37
02:00.767 --> 02:02.727
What, "scam you"? "Steal from you"?

38
02:02.811 --> 02:05.355
[in English] Are you kidding me? Look at your destruction.

39
02:05.439 --> 02:07.107
And you ate all my strawberries.

40
02:07.190 --> 02:08.191
[in Korean] What…

41
02:09.234 --> 02:11.278
Seriously. Man, this is frustrating.

42
02:11.361 --> 02:13.697
Look, you got it all wrong. These strawberries were…

43
02:13.780 --> 02:14.865
[groans]

44
02:14.948 --> 02:16.575
[in English] You owe me an explanation.

45
02:17.159 --> 02:20.120
[on phone, children clamoring]

46
02:22.831 --> 02:26.418
[child cheering] Thank you.

47
02:30.005 --> 02:31.965
[in Korean] What'd I tell you, huh? I… Right.

48
02:32.966 --> 02:33.967
Here.

49
02:34.718 --> 02:36.178
I told you it wasn't me.

50
02:36.261 --> 02:37.888
I TOLD YOU IT WASN'T ME.

51
02:40.599 --> 02:43.685
[in English] Well… Okay… Tell me what you're doing here then.

52
02:44.227 --> 02:45.520
[in Korean] I own this property.

53
02:47.939 --> 02:49.566
[in English] What? [scoffs]

54
02:49.649 --> 02:51.610
What would my farm be doing here

55
02:51.693 --> 02:54.112
if you were the owner, huh? That doesn't make sense does it?

56
02:55.655 --> 02:56.782
[chuckles]

57
02:57.699 --> 02:59.242
[in Korean] Geez, ugh.

58
03:00.577 --> 03:01.787
Here, look at this.

59
03:03.747 --> 03:06.249
Read this, okay? Look.

60
03:08.919 --> 03:09.920
I mean…

61
03:10.670 --> 03:12.589
Technically, you're the thief here.

62
03:13.089 --> 03:16.301
You're growing crops on someone else's property without permission.

63
03:17.844 --> 03:20.096
[♪ comical music plays]

64
03:26.686 --> 03:27.687
[in English] Huh?

65
03:30.315 --> 03:31.399
[in Korean] Wait…

66
03:32.359 --> 03:34.402
Why is there a…

67
03:34.486 --> 03:36.196
[officer, in English] See this tiny spot?

68
03:36.821 --> 03:38.823
You don't own this lot here.

69
03:40.116 --> 03:45.372
This specific plot is owned by Ms. Shirahama Karin. Hmm?

70
03:45.455 --> 03:46.665
[sighs]

71
03:46.748 --> 03:50.627
-Huh? M-Ms. Karin? Shirahama Karin? -[officer] Mm-hmm.

72
03:50.710 --> 03:51.878
[Yubin] Ms. Karin…

73
03:53.004 --> 03:55.340
In other words, it's my property.

74
03:56.508 --> 04:00.053
"My… My property"?

75
04:01.888 --> 04:06.643
You walked onto my private property and you single-handedly ruined everything.

76
04:10.564 --> 04:12.440
Ah… [sighs]

77
04:12.524 --> 04:13.775
[in Korean] No, that's…

78
04:15.443 --> 04:18.029
I mean, it's not like I did it on purpose.

79
04:20.407 --> 04:23.702
I mean, you can't go calling me a thief over eating one lousy strawberry.

80
04:25.579 --> 04:27.747
YOU CAN'T GO CALLING ME A THIEF

81
04:27.831 --> 04:29.499
OVER EATING ONE LOUSY STRAWBERRY

82
04:31.668 --> 04:33.879
[in English, sighs] "One lousy strawberry"?

83
04:35.672 --> 04:37.424
[scoffs, sighs]

84
04:37.507 --> 04:39.634
That is the rudest thing I've ever heard.

85
04:40.385 --> 04:41.386
[in Korean] Hey, wait.

86
04:44.347 --> 04:48.226
[in English] Excuse me. We're closed. It's after 5 o'clock.

87
04:49.978 --> 04:51.062
[Yubin] Uh…

88
04:52.230 --> 04:54.691
[in Korean] Seriously, I can't understand a thing they're saying.

89
04:55.859 --> 04:57.152
Wait a minute.

90
04:57.235 --> 04:58.695
Hey, I said wait.

91
04:58.778 --> 05:00.030
Wait.

92
05:02.365 --> 05:03.825
[sighs]

93
05:06.036 --> 05:07.621
I'll make it all up to you.

94
05:09.539 --> 05:12.751
[in English] Oh, yeah? [chuckles] You gonna go back in time or what?

95
05:13.543 --> 05:16.588
[in Korean] I don't have the time to waste on you right now, okay?

96
05:17.714 --> 05:19.382
[in English] Just leave me alone.

97
05:20.050 --> 05:21.927
You can't fix anything, so leave.

98
05:23.970 --> 05:25.013
CHARO VILLAGE OFFICE

99
05:25.096 --> 05:26.556
[in Korean] Fine, just go.

100
05:27.390 --> 05:29.434
I was just trying to be nice.

101
05:30.352 --> 05:31.519
Fine!

102
05:35.815 --> 05:37.108
Where the heck am I?

103
05:40.236 --> 05:42.405
Man… I missed my flight.

104
05:45.116 --> 05:48.078
[in English] Kunam, close up the shop tonight, will ya?

105
05:48.161 --> 05:49.454
CHARO ISLAND'S ONLY ASAHI STORE

106
05:49.537 --> 05:51.289
-Yes, sir. -Mmm.

107
05:55.794 --> 05:58.713
-Mari, would you like to go for a walk? -[door closes]

108
06:01.299 --> 06:03.009
Let's go for a walk.

109
06:03.927 --> 06:06.137
-Let's walk a little. -Why are you being weird?

110
06:09.474 --> 06:11.851
Wanna go for… a walk?

111
06:11.935 --> 06:12.936
I'll pass.

112
06:13.019 --> 06:15.188
-I'm honestly a little wiped out. -You're tired?

113
06:16.648 --> 06:19.067
I know an energy drink that will wake you up instantly.

114
06:19.776 --> 06:21.403
[phone buzzing]

115
06:21.486 --> 06:23.947
-I'll let you take that. -Oh.

116
06:24.030 --> 06:25.115
Mari…

117
06:25.198 --> 06:26.408
Wait a sec.

118
06:31.955 --> 06:33.665
[Yubin, in Korean] Come to the village office.

119
06:33.748 --> 06:34.916
Why should I?

120
06:36.001 --> 06:37.293
I'll pay you.

121
06:37.377 --> 06:38.420
[scoffs]

122
06:42.257 --> 06:44.759
A LEISURELY ISLAND LIFE RESIDENTS WELCOME!

123
06:49.889 --> 06:50.890
[♪ whimsical music plays]

124
06:50.974 --> 06:51.975
Huh?

125
06:53.518 --> 06:54.728
I'm not some weirdo.

126
06:55.437 --> 06:57.939
See, the thing is, I'm actually…

127
06:58.440 --> 07:01.776
So, you see… I am a properly vetted individual.

128
07:01.860 --> 07:04.237
Let me show you. Here, take a look.

129
07:04.320 --> 07:05.321
LEE YUBIN - SPATIAL DESIGNER

130
07:05.405 --> 07:07.031
You can search me up. Yeah, you see that?

131
07:07.115 --> 07:08.324
That's who I am.

132
07:08.992 --> 07:10.243
Got it? Here, look.

133
07:10.326 --> 07:12.036
A RISING STAR FALLEN: INVESTORS RAISE OBJECTION

134
07:12.120 --> 07:13.455
Says your company went bust.

135
07:15.039 --> 07:16.416
Exactly, so please buy me dinner.

136
07:16.499 --> 07:17.709
Me?

137
07:18.752 --> 07:20.044
I'll pay you back in one go.

138
07:21.212 --> 07:24.007
[♪ amusing music playing]

139
07:25.383 --> 07:26.426
Double.

140
07:36.269 --> 07:38.146
[♪ synth-pop music playing]

141
07:47.071 --> 07:48.072
What is this place?

142
07:48.156 --> 07:50.867
NOW OFFERING FATEFUL CURRY OF LOVE

143
07:52.035 --> 07:54.162
[in English] Mari's "Fateful Curry of Love,"

144
07:54.245 --> 07:55.497
made from the heart.

145
07:55.580 --> 07:58.792
-Please enjoy! -Thank you very much.

146
07:58.875 --> 08:00.376
-Mm-hmm. -Uh…

147
08:01.628 --> 08:03.129
[in Korean] Okay, so…

148
08:03.838 --> 08:04.923
What did she say?

149
08:05.006 --> 08:06.508
She said shut up and eat.

150
08:12.847 --> 08:13.932
Ah…

151
08:16.935 --> 08:19.437
[in English] Hey, who's this charming guy?

152
08:20.396 --> 08:22.565
"Charming guy"? Oh. Who, me?

153
08:22.649 --> 08:24.025
[groans]

154
08:28.446 --> 08:30.365
-It's great. [chuckles] -It's… It's great?

155
08:30.448 --> 08:31.658
-It's great. Mmm. -[laughs] It's great.

156
08:31.741 --> 08:33.910
-Thank you very much. -Okay, okay, that's enough.

157
08:33.993 --> 08:36.704
Ugh, stop it. Where are we going?

158
08:36.788 --> 08:39.457
-You said you're tired. -No. Hang on a second, I'm fine now.

159
08:39.541 --> 08:41.543
-Hey. No, wait. -Bye-bye.

160
08:42.126 --> 08:45.964
[♪ amusing music playing]

161
08:53.930 --> 08:56.099
[in Korean] If you're done eating, pay up and go.

162
08:58.268 --> 08:59.519
Come on, Kunam.

163
09:00.061 --> 09:02.605
I'm not even halfway done. Don't be so heartless, will you?

164
09:02.689 --> 09:03.731
Have a seat real quick.

165
09:10.071 --> 09:11.447
[clears throat]

166
09:11.531 --> 09:12.782
Okay, so…

167
09:13.658 --> 09:15.702
Tell me, Kunam.

168
09:15.785 --> 09:16.786
How old are you?

169
09:17.704 --> 09:19.164
-I'm 27. -Mmm.

170
09:19.247 --> 09:21.583
Sounds about right. I'm older, so I'll drop the formalities.

171
09:21.666 --> 09:22.709
I'd rather you didn't.

172
09:22.792 --> 09:25.962
Hey, Kunam, I know it's been tough for you, all alone in a foreign country.

173
09:26.045 --> 09:27.255
Well, you must be lonely.

174
09:27.755 --> 09:29.299
-No, I'm not. -Of course you are.

175
09:30.049 --> 09:31.843
But not tonight. Not with me here for you.

176
09:32.343 --> 09:33.553
Where should we go?

177
09:34.262 --> 09:35.263
"We"?

178
09:36.806 --> 09:38.224
Let me crash at yours just for one night.

179
09:40.185 --> 09:41.728
Just for the night, please.

180
09:41.811 --> 09:45.398
[dog howling]

181
09:49.944 --> 09:52.488
[in English] "One lousy strawberry," he said…

182
09:55.909 --> 09:59.329
Does he even know how many years I've poured into each strawberry?

183
10:06.419 --> 10:09.130
[smartwatch chiming]

184
10:10.632 --> 10:12.008
-[sighs] -[chiming stops]

185
10:20.516 --> 10:22.518
[♪ melancholy music playing]

186
10:23.102 --> 10:24.103
[sighs]

187
10:56.010 --> 10:57.345
[in Korean] See you never.

188
11:04.477 --> 11:06.479
[♪ ethereal music playing]

189
11:08.022 --> 11:09.190
[alarm beeping]

190
11:09.274 --> 11:11.609
KARIN'S DAILY CHART

191
11:19.284 --> 11:20.285
[beeping stops]

192
11:33.965 --> 11:36.467
[electronic beeping]

193
11:50.606 --> 11:52.358
-[in English] All right, all right. -[beeping stops]

194
12:11.669 --> 12:13.379
[♪ melancholy music playing]

195
12:20.803 --> 12:22.013
[birds chirping]

196
12:36.569 --> 12:37.570
[sighs]

197
12:39.572 --> 12:42.825
It's impossible. There's no way I can do this alone.

198
13:13.231 --> 13:14.232
[sighs]

199
13:25.118 --> 13:26.119
[sighs]

200
13:29.747 --> 13:31.290
How do I do this?

201
13:42.343 --> 13:43.344
[person] Karin.

202
13:44.804 --> 13:45.805
Karin.

203
13:49.642 --> 13:51.894
Isn't it past your bedtime?

204
13:51.978 --> 13:52.979
Go to bed.

205
13:55.982 --> 13:56.983
Grandpa…

206
13:58.609 --> 14:00.486
[sighs] There isn't enough time as it is.

207
14:00.570 --> 14:02.238
I shouldn't be wasting it sleeping.

208
14:04.157 --> 14:07.869
It seems like I've caused you so much trouble. I'm sorry.

209
14:09.328 --> 14:10.538
It's too much, isn't it?

210
14:10.621 --> 14:13.040
I won't blame you if you want to give up.

211
14:13.124 --> 14:15.084
Grandpa, I'm not giving up on this.

212
14:15.710 --> 14:17.712
Not when this farm is your dream.

213
14:18.713 --> 14:19.714
No way.

214
14:23.009 --> 14:25.011
Look how you've grown.

215
14:25.094 --> 14:27.221
What a sweet girl you are.

216
14:27.805 --> 14:29.348
Sweeter than a strawberry.

217
14:31.893 --> 14:32.894
I'm failing.

218
14:35.605 --> 14:36.689
Karin.

219
14:37.857 --> 14:39.525
Don't worry so much.

220
14:39.609 --> 14:42.403
The path you've been on is the right one.

221
14:51.787 --> 14:52.788
[Karin] Grandpa…

222
15:09.513 --> 15:10.848
[teacher] Excuse me!

223
15:11.724 --> 15:12.934
Sorry to bother you.

224
15:22.568 --> 15:26.572
We are so incredibly sorry for all the trouble we've caused you.

225
15:28.449 --> 15:30.993
I promise we'll make up for what we've done,

226
15:31.077 --> 15:33.120
and we hope that you can forgive us.

227
15:33.704 --> 15:36.832
[children] We're really sorry!

228
15:39.502 --> 15:43.130
Your strawberries were the best that I ever had.

229
15:43.214 --> 15:46.801
Yeah, the strawberries on your farm are number one.

230
15:46.884 --> 15:50.972
This might be overstepping, but I just wanted to let you know

231
15:51.055 --> 15:53.933
that the children had the time of their lives that day.

232
15:59.647 --> 16:01.816
THANK YOU FOR THE DELICIOUS STRAWBERRIES

233
16:04.151 --> 16:06.237
I want more strawberries!

234
16:06.320 --> 16:07.530
-Yeah! Me too! -Me three!

235
16:07.613 --> 16:09.448
-More! I want more strawberries! -I want more!

236
16:09.532 --> 16:11.033
-Please, lady. -Please, Miss.

237
16:11.117 --> 16:13.286
-Please! -Please, I wanna come back!

238
16:13.369 --> 16:15.579
-Please, please! -I want more of your strawberries!

239
16:15.663 --> 16:19.000
[clamoring continues]

240
16:20.710 --> 16:22.003
Thank you all. [chuckles]

241
16:22.670 --> 16:25.006
I promise you'll get more strawberries later.

242
16:25.089 --> 16:27.591
[children] Yay! Thank you!

243
16:27.675 --> 16:30.428
[cheering, clamoring continues]

244
16:30.511 --> 16:32.096
[child] I want more strawberries!

245
16:32.179 --> 16:34.807
[children] Yay! Thank you!

246
16:34.890 --> 16:37.059
[in Korean] I feel like it's going to sell fine.

247
16:37.143 --> 16:38.811
But then again, maybe it won't.

248
16:38.894 --> 16:41.188
Man, I really hope it sells…

249
16:41.897 --> 16:42.898
This land…

250
16:42.982 --> 16:45.735
Man, it's not going to sell, is it? How am I going to sell this land?

251
16:45.818 --> 16:46.819
I'll just…

252
16:46.902 --> 16:48.654
No, I have to sell it no matter what.

253
16:48.738 --> 16:49.905
Man, but how?

254
16:49.989 --> 16:53.117
Would you just sit down and wait? You're getting on my nerves!

255
16:53.200 --> 16:55.619
Well, I seriously have to sell this land! I have to, no matter what!

256
16:55.703 --> 16:57.663
I'll sell it off to get back on my feet!

257
16:57.747 --> 17:00.333
Hyejin. Can't you feel it? Don't you see?

258
17:00.416 --> 17:02.793
The entire world's waiting for my comeback.

259
17:02.877 --> 17:04.211
I genuinely don't see it.

260
17:04.795 --> 17:06.255
-You don't? -No.

261
17:06.339 --> 17:08.674
-Now sit. -No, I…

262
17:08.758 --> 17:11.010
Huh? Hey, talk to me, Sanggi. How did it go?

263
17:11.093 --> 17:12.219
-Hey. -Did it sell?

264
17:12.303 --> 17:15.306
-Well? Did it? -Huh? No. It didn't.

265
17:19.352 --> 17:22.396
Yeah, of course it didn't. I knew it.

266
17:22.480 --> 17:23.731
-I mean, yeah… -No, wait…

267
17:23.814 --> 17:24.940
I knew he wouldn't buy.

268
17:25.024 --> 17:27.610
Did you see the look on his face? I knew he wouldn't buy it.

269
17:28.110 --> 17:29.820
-I had the worst dream last night. -Hey…

270
17:29.904 --> 17:32.198
-Gosh, it was so unsettling, you know… -Yubin.

271
17:32.281 --> 17:33.658
Look at this, okay?

272
17:33.741 --> 17:38.120
You know that plot of land that belongs to that Karin person?

273
17:38.204 --> 17:40.498
Yeah? This bit right here is the sweet spot.

274
17:40.581 --> 17:42.375
This plot right here leads to the piers.

275
17:42.458 --> 17:45.878
You have to secure this lot to make your land worth it.

276
17:45.961 --> 17:48.923
-Yeah? -Tell me something I don't know.

277
17:49.006 --> 17:51.092
Hey, so listen, yeah?

278
17:51.175 --> 17:53.511
How about you just buy it yourself?

279
17:54.637 --> 17:57.306
You can pay it off when you sell your land anyway.

280
17:57.390 --> 17:59.809
If I were you, I'd buy it in a heartbeat.

281
17:59.892 --> 18:02.061
This right here. Yeah.

282
18:06.148 --> 18:07.191
-I've got to go. -Oh, gosh.

283
18:07.274 --> 18:09.026
Geez, where are you off to now?

284
18:09.110 --> 18:10.111
Charo Island.

285
18:10.194 --> 18:11.237
[Hyejin] To do what exactly?

286
18:11.320 --> 18:13.030
Well, I have to secure that land somehow!

287
18:13.114 --> 18:14.907
I have to coax that girl into selling it off.

288
18:14.990 --> 18:16.742
That's the only way I can get back on my feet.

289
18:16.826 --> 18:18.619
I'll just slide right in, and…

290
18:18.703 --> 18:20.496
-Hey, Yubin. Get a grip. -I'll be real smooth…

291
18:20.579 --> 18:22.456
Didn't you say you got into a big fight with her?

292
18:22.540 --> 18:28.129
Look, people fight. That's how you get close and build a bond.

293
18:28.212 --> 18:29.922
-That's true. Yeah. -Okay, Sanggi, Hyejin.

294
18:30.005 --> 18:31.674
I'll be right back with the land. Just wait.

295
18:31.757 --> 18:34.677
-Hey, Lee Yubin. Lee Yubin? -Go get 'em!

296
18:34.760 --> 18:37.054
-[Hyejin] Hey, stop enabling him. -[Sanggi] Wow, he's fast.

297
18:37.138 --> 18:38.139
TAX ACCOUNTANT CHOI HYEJIN

298
18:51.193 --> 18:52.528
-[tap opens] -[water spraying]

299
18:52.611 --> 18:53.988
[screaming]

300
18:55.489 --> 18:56.699
[Kunam, in English] Mari.

301
18:58.409 --> 19:00.411
Mari, hang on!

302
19:01.120 --> 19:02.329
Oh, no. Help me.

303
19:02.413 --> 19:03.414
I'll handle it.

304
19:03.497 --> 19:04.707
[Mari whimpers] Kunam!

305
19:04.790 --> 19:07.251
-Whoa! -[screams] Kunam, you're making it worse!

306
19:07.334 --> 19:08.669
-Hey, wait! -[Kunam] Oh, no!

307
19:08.753 --> 19:11.297
-[Karin] You're flooding my whole field! -[Mari] Kunam.

308
19:11.380 --> 19:12.882
Turn off the water supply, Kunam.

309
19:12.965 --> 19:15.426
-Over there! -[in Korean] Oh, right… The water!

310
19:15.509 --> 19:16.886
[Mari whining]

311
19:16.969 --> 19:19.555
-[Mari, screaming] What do I do? -[Kunam] Oh, no, how do I turn this off?

312
19:19.638 --> 19:21.390
[in English] This is a disaster.

313
19:21.891 --> 19:24.059
-[phone buzzing] -[sighs]

314
19:25.227 --> 19:27.313
[grunts] Karin speaking.

315
19:28.355 --> 19:29.440
Yes?

316
19:29.940 --> 19:31.776
Someone is interested? [gasps]

317
19:31.859 --> 19:33.444
Interested in what?

318
19:33.527 --> 19:36.280
-In working here! -[Mari, Kunam cheering]

319
19:36.363 --> 19:38.115
[Karin] Thank you so much!

320
19:38.199 --> 19:41.452
-[Mari] I'm so over this hard labor! -Great. Yes.

321
19:41.535 --> 19:43.496
[chuckling] Yes!

322
19:43.579 --> 19:45.664
WELCOME TO ODAIRA DISTRICT

323
19:45.748 --> 19:48.626
No matter what you do, don't overwork this one.

324
19:48.709 --> 19:50.669
Don't let him even think of running away.

325
19:50.753 --> 19:52.880
I swear that I'll be nicer to this one.

326
19:52.963 --> 19:54.006
-Trust me, okay? -Mm-hmm.

327
19:56.091 --> 19:58.093
-[gasps] There he is! Here he comes! -[squeals]

328
19:58.177 --> 20:00.971
-[Mari] He's here! [gasps] -[squeals, chuckles]

329
20:01.055 --> 20:03.516
[♪ Spanish guitar music playing]

330
20:10.481 --> 20:11.482
[Karin gasps]

331
20:12.066 --> 20:15.152
[both chuckling]

332
20:31.502 --> 20:33.170
What? Huh?

333
20:42.888 --> 20:44.431
[in Korean] What is it that she needs?

334
21:08.163 --> 21:09.498
A man.

335
21:11.250 --> 21:12.418
A man?

336
21:16.046 --> 21:18.382
I knew it. See? When I first saw her,

337
21:18.465 --> 21:21.176
she was having this weird conversation with that foreign dude. I swear.

338
21:21.260 --> 21:23.387
-That's not what I meant. -Then what?

339
21:23.470 --> 21:26.015
What Karin needs is a sagyou-in.

340
21:26.098 --> 21:28.309
What's a sagyou-in?

341
21:28.893 --> 21:31.061
A strapping male laborer.

342
21:31.645 --> 21:33.939
What? A male laborer?

343
21:34.815 --> 21:35.941
[grunts]

344
21:38.485 --> 21:40.195
[in English] You're the new field worker?

345
21:41.071 --> 21:42.281
Mm-hmm. Field worker.

346
21:42.364 --> 21:44.241
Is this some kind of joke?

347
21:46.827 --> 21:49.830
As your new field hand, I'll do whatever you need.

348
21:50.331 --> 21:52.458
[sighs] I'd rather do all of this work on my own.

349
21:52.541 --> 21:53.667
[Mari] Yeah, right. [scoffs]

350
21:53.751 --> 21:55.836
Karin, you can't do this alone.

351
21:55.920 --> 21:57.671
-Yeah, I know but-- -Dig potatoes,

352
21:57.755 --> 22:01.133
grow strawberries, dig carrots, pack them, send them out…

353
22:01.216 --> 22:04.094
[gasps] Are you planning to force me and Kunam to do it?

354
22:04.178 --> 22:05.554
But it's this guy.

355
22:07.765 --> 22:09.475
He's your only option.

356
22:09.558 --> 22:12.645
He doesn't look like he's touched dirt in his entire life.

357
22:12.728 --> 22:14.480
Beggars can't be choosers.

358
22:15.940 --> 22:17.816
I think he'll be good enough.

359
22:20.235 --> 22:21.695
I'll give it all I've got.

360
22:23.614 --> 22:24.907
Let's do this.

361
22:26.992 --> 22:28.911
[in Korean] I have a bad feeling about this.

362
22:33.165 --> 22:35.376
How much further up does this trail even go?

363
22:36.085 --> 22:37.795
-Whatever, it's nothing. -[animals howling]

364
22:37.878 --> 22:40.005
What is this place? It's like it's haunted or something.

365
22:40.506 --> 22:41.674
Oh.

366
22:41.757 --> 22:43.842
Hey, wait up!

367
22:50.349 --> 22:52.184
[in English] This is where you're staying.

368
23:01.110 --> 23:02.611
THIS IS YOUR LODGING.

369
23:05.239 --> 23:07.324
Or you can leave if you hate it.

370
23:14.748 --> 23:16.333
[in Korean] No, I just…

371
23:16.417 --> 23:18.168
Actually, I just wanted to

372
23:19.253 --> 23:23.674
take in the whole place from a distance.

373
23:23.757 --> 23:26.093
I love the look of this place. It's…

374
23:26.677 --> 23:27.845
very vintage.

375
23:27.928 --> 23:29.847
[in English] Don't be late tomorrow.

376
23:31.890 --> 23:33.392
Bright and early, Boss.

377
23:33.976 --> 23:35.561
He won't last one night.

378
23:41.567 --> 23:43.110
[in Korean] Oh, man.

379
23:44.361 --> 23:45.362
[scoffs]

380
23:46.030 --> 23:49.241
I'm very picky when it comes to where I sleep, though. Geez.

381
23:56.582 --> 23:59.501
[rooster crows]

382
24:06.216 --> 24:07.593
[in English] Rise and shine.

383
24:08.469 --> 24:09.928
[in Korean] What the…

384
24:10.012 --> 24:11.388
[in English] Hear what I said?

385
24:12.973 --> 24:14.391
[in Korean] It's six…

386
24:14.892 --> 24:16.393
It's six o'clock.

387
24:16.477 --> 24:18.562
[in English] Stop being lazy.

388
24:19.813 --> 24:21.065
[whimpers]

389
24:21.899 --> 24:24.193
-[groans] -No sleeping.

390
24:24.276 --> 24:25.277
Get up!

391
24:25.360 --> 24:27.321
[groans] Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.

392
24:27.404 --> 24:28.447
I'm awake.

393
24:28.530 --> 24:31.366
[♪ spaghetti Western music playing]

394
24:41.210 --> 24:42.211
Test 1.

395
24:43.128 --> 24:45.339
Show me how you till soil. Come on.

396
24:45.964 --> 24:47.883
-Test 1? -Test 1.

397
24:47.966 --> 24:48.967
Okay.

398
24:49.051 --> 24:50.344
[snickers, scoffs]

399
24:50.844 --> 24:52.262
[in Korean] You want to test me, huh?

400
24:52.346 --> 24:54.890
I've done on-site work for years.

401
24:56.767 --> 24:58.685
Guess a field this big would take about…

402
24:59.853 --> 25:01.063
Well…

403
25:01.146 --> 25:02.231
Fifteen minutes?

404
25:05.192 --> 25:06.652
All right. [grunting]

405
25:10.864 --> 25:12.074
[scoffs]

406
25:14.576 --> 25:16.495
Oh, man!

407
25:17.913 --> 25:20.207
[grunting, straining]

408
25:22.709 --> 25:26.171
[in English] I asked you to till the soil, not completely destroy it.

409
25:26.255 --> 25:28.507
[in English] Unbelievable. [scoffs]

410
25:28.590 --> 25:30.551
[whines, exclaims]

411
25:32.136 --> 25:34.096
[Karin] You know what a weed is, right?

412
25:39.268 --> 25:40.269
[grunts]

413
25:40.769 --> 25:44.064
[in Korean] Aha! Got myself a big one. [chuckles]

414
25:44.148 --> 25:46.984
[in English] That's not a weed. That is a sweet potato.

415
25:47.568 --> 25:48.694
[sighs]

416
25:49.278 --> 25:50.279
[yawns]

417
25:51.280 --> 25:53.740
You need to pick the bugs off of the leaves.

418
25:53.824 --> 25:55.200
-Huh? -[scoffs]

419
25:55.284 --> 25:59.288
I said, "You need to get the bugs."

420
25:59.371 --> 26:00.873
-Look. The bugs. -Huh? What?

421
26:00.956 --> 26:02.457
-Oh. Bugs. -Right.

422
26:02.541 --> 26:06.128
-With your hands, pick up the bugs. -Pick?

423
26:06.211 --> 26:07.337
-Pick. -Right. Pick.

424
26:09.298 --> 26:10.841
[in Korean] Where are these bugs?

425
26:11.717 --> 26:15.262
I don't see any. Oh. [grunts]

426
26:19.266 --> 26:23.020
-[screaming] Man. A bug! -[gasps]

427
26:23.729 --> 26:27.858
A bug! Ew!

428
26:32.321 --> 26:33.822
Listen, you know that girl, Karin?

429
26:33.906 --> 26:36.533
Carl? Whatever her name is, I'm telling you, she's totally crazy.

430
26:36.617 --> 26:38.827
Huh? Hey, will you listen to me for a second?

431
26:38.911 --> 26:42.372
I mean, I know I'm here to work for her, but she made me sleep in the shed!

432
26:42.456 --> 26:44.750
I haven't had a single good night's sleep since I got here.

433
26:44.833 --> 26:47.002
She just throws me a few steamed sweet potatoes, and then…

434
26:47.085 --> 26:49.880
Listen! Then she worked me like a dog from 6 a.m. in the morning until now!

435
26:49.963 --> 26:51.924
Did you think farm work would be a walk in the park?

436
26:52.007 --> 26:55.552
I know it's not a walk in the park! But she's just way over the line! Geez.

437
26:55.636 --> 26:57.054
And you know what else?

438
26:57.846 --> 26:59.681
I think she's taking something.

439
27:00.849 --> 27:03.101
She must be hoarding all the good stuff for herself.

440
27:03.185 --> 27:05.062
She's so tiny, but her stamina is crazy.

441
27:05.145 --> 27:07.481
See, there's a reason behind that.

442
27:08.482 --> 27:09.775
What is it?

443
27:11.068 --> 27:13.070
Karin is actually a bit unwell.

444
27:14.363 --> 27:16.365
That's why everyone here looks out for her.

445
27:19.826 --> 27:21.370
Is that what it is?

446
27:21.453 --> 27:24.247
Hang in there, man. Nothing comes easy in life.

447
27:28.543 --> 27:29.544
What's this?

448
27:29.628 --> 27:31.129
A Japanese textbook?

449
27:31.213 --> 27:32.756
NEW JAPANESE FOR TOTAL BEGINNERS

450
27:32.839 --> 27:34.883
This is what got me where I am right now.

451
27:34.967 --> 27:37.344
Doesn't really seem like a great place to be.

452
27:37.886 --> 27:41.139
Come on, man. You said you had to get on her good side.

453
27:41.223 --> 27:44.226
Then, you must be able to talk to her. You can't use a translator app forever.

454
27:44.309 --> 27:47.229
I should probably study some Japanese, right?

455
27:48.105 --> 27:50.983
[in English] "Excuse me. Where are you going?"

456
27:51.066 --> 27:52.567
[in Korean] That'll be 30,000 won.

457
27:57.280 --> 28:00.033
[in English] "What is today's date?"

458
28:00.117 --> 28:01.868
[in Korean] Come on, man. Please buy one off me.

459
28:02.869 --> 28:04.705
It's used. Give me a little discount.

460
28:05.414 --> 28:07.499
[in English] "It's good to meet you."

461
28:08.458 --> 28:11.253
"It's a pleasure to meet you as well."

462
28:11.753 --> 28:12.963
[in Korean] What's this?

463
28:15.507 --> 28:16.508
Huh?

464
28:18.468 --> 28:21.304
Wait, seriously? More sweet potatoes?

465
28:23.098 --> 28:24.099
What's this?

466
28:24.182 --> 28:26.518
YASUMI PASS-A HIGH ABSORPTION MENTHOL COMPOUND

467
28:31.898 --> 28:33.275
Does she think she can…

468
28:35.861 --> 28:37.654
win me over that easily?

469
28:49.916 --> 28:51.710
THAT'S NOT A NOTEBOOK.

470
29:01.470 --> 29:04.389
[in English] One, two, three, four.

471
29:05.307 --> 29:08.143
SHIRAHAMA

472
29:09.436 --> 29:11.480
Ah. Hi there. Good morning.

473
29:12.272 --> 29:13.273
Morning.

474
29:15.233 --> 29:17.569
Well, um… hmm…

475
29:18.070 --> 29:20.197
So, uh…

476
29:20.822 --> 29:21.823
Hmm.

477
29:22.407 --> 29:24.117
[in Korean] Man, I forgot.

478
29:25.410 --> 29:26.787
Where should we start today?

479
29:27.788 --> 29:28.789
[in English] Ah.

480
29:30.582 --> 29:32.209
Start with the fertilizer…

481
29:35.337 --> 29:38.215
No. Focus on the weeding today.

482
29:38.298 --> 29:40.967
Don't pull out anything you're not sure of. Got it?

483
29:42.636 --> 29:44.888
[in Korean] Wait, what? I thought we were working together today.

484
29:46.098 --> 29:47.933
[sighs, speaks English] I have an errand to run.

485
29:48.016 --> 29:49.351
[in Korean] Huh? What…

486
29:57.943 --> 29:59.778
[in English] I have to do something.

487
30:04.908 --> 30:06.118
[in Korean] Huh, what…

488
30:17.003 --> 30:18.338
If only…

489
30:20.674 --> 30:21.675
[sighs]

490
30:21.758 --> 30:24.177
I could have this little lot.

491
30:25.887 --> 30:26.972
[sucks teeth]

492
30:27.514 --> 30:29.724
But why was she in such a bad mood?

493
30:31.852 --> 30:34.396
[sucks teeth] Could it be because of this field?

494
30:35.772 --> 30:38.358
Wait, why are they all wilting like this?

495
30:41.611 --> 30:42.904
Wait a minute.

496
30:46.449 --> 30:49.578
WHEN STRAWBERRY PLANTS WILT

497
30:49.661 --> 30:50.662
REMOVE THE WEAKER PLANTS,

498
30:50.745 --> 30:52.205
CONTROL THE IRRIGATION, AND IMPROVE SOIL.

499
30:52.289 --> 30:53.790
SEASHELL FERTILIZER HELPS YIELD FIRMER STRAWBERRIES!

500
30:53.874 --> 30:55.125
"Calcium."

501
30:55.792 --> 30:57.502
"Strawberry fertilizer."

502
30:57.586 --> 31:00.338
FERTILIZER EFFECTIVE FOR GROWING STRAWBERRIES

503
31:00.422 --> 31:01.423
Uh-huh.

504
31:01.506 --> 31:04.926
CALCIUM IN SHELL FERTILIZER IMPROVES QUALITY AND YIELD

505
31:05.010 --> 31:06.052
Okay.

506
31:07.888 --> 31:09.055
Let's give it a go.

507
31:15.270 --> 31:16.479
[strains]

508
31:17.314 --> 31:20.275
[grunts] Oh, there it is.

509
31:21.735 --> 31:22.736
Ugh, my legs.

510
31:26.698 --> 31:29.075
NO ILLEGAL FISHING FUNAURA FISHING UNION

511
31:29.159 --> 31:30.368
Now…

512
31:31.912 --> 31:34.122
Wow, okay.

513
31:34.748 --> 31:36.374
This should be enough, right?

514
31:37.000 --> 31:38.168
[strains]

515
31:38.251 --> 31:39.669
My foot keeps getting stuck. Geez.

516
31:41.922 --> 31:43.089
[sighs]

517
31:44.299 --> 31:46.051
[in English] What are you doing here?

518
31:47.427 --> 31:49.221
[in Korean] Hey, how'd you know I was here?

519
31:50.388 --> 31:52.057
Boss! Look at this!

520
31:52.140 --> 31:55.143
-Look, I caught all of these. -[in English] Why are you out here

521
31:55.227 --> 31:57.687
gathering seashells and not doing the weeding?

522
31:58.480 --> 32:00.190
-Huh? -[sighs]

523
32:00.815 --> 32:02.984
You're not allowed to do this here.

524
32:03.068 --> 32:04.903
-Come on. Let's… -[whistle blowing]

525
32:05.820 --> 32:08.990
-Hey! This is a legally protected area! -We need to run!

526
32:09.074 --> 32:10.325
-Ready? Run! -[in Korean] What?

527
32:10.408 --> 32:11.660
-[stammers] -[in English] Run! Run!

528
32:11.743 --> 32:13.703
[Yubin, in Korean] I'm stuck! I can't move!

529
32:13.787 --> 32:15.205
[both grunting]

530
32:15.288 --> 32:17.040
[whistle blowing]

531
32:17.123 --> 32:19.000
[♪ Spanish guitar music playing]

532
32:19.084 --> 32:20.377
[in English] Get unstuck!

533
32:45.318 --> 32:46.319
[music ends]

534
32:46.403 --> 32:48.697
[in Korean] Well, how was I supposed to know this was illegal?

535
32:52.200 --> 32:54.953
[in English] Who told you to come out here and find shells?

536
32:58.832 --> 33:01.376
[in Korean] I mean, you seemed a little troubled.

537
33:03.962 --> 33:07.257
I thought it might be because of the strawberries,

538
33:07.340 --> 33:09.384
so I wanted to help out.

539
33:12.804 --> 33:14.889
[shakes out bag]

540
33:14.973 --> 33:17.100
[♪ romantic music playing]

541
33:19.060 --> 33:20.186
So, hey.

542
33:21.354 --> 33:23.565
It's fine if we just take a few of these back with us, right?

543
33:25.108 --> 33:26.401
[in English] No way.

544
33:27.110 --> 33:30.155
[stammers, speaks Korean] I guess I shouldn't, huh?

545
33:31.406 --> 33:32.657
[gasps, laughs]

546
33:37.454 --> 33:39.331
Mm-hmm. Okay, okay, okay.

547
33:39.914 --> 33:41.124
This is all of them.

548
33:41.207 --> 33:42.208
[in English] Wow.

549
33:43.293 --> 33:44.919
[in Korean] I was hoping to pocket a few.

550
33:45.837 --> 33:47.130
-There. -[laughs]

551
33:50.008 --> 33:51.051
That's it. There's no more.

552
33:52.594 --> 33:54.429
-[in English] None? -[grunts] None, none.

553
33:54.512 --> 33:55.722
None, none, none.

554
33:55.805 --> 33:57.307
[in Korean] None left. Mmm.

555
34:03.897 --> 34:05.523
[wobbles]

556
34:05.607 --> 34:07.192
[laughing]

557
34:10.695 --> 34:12.405
[Karin, in English] I almost fell!

558
34:12.489 --> 34:15.367
[both laughing]

559
34:22.207 --> 34:23.208
[music ends]

560
34:23.291 --> 34:24.334
[sighs]

561
34:27.379 --> 34:28.713
[in Korean] Hey, so…

562
34:28.797 --> 34:30.382
Right. [grunts]

563
34:33.176 --> 34:34.677
About the strawberries.

564
34:38.014 --> 34:40.975
Don't people usually grow strawberries in greenhouses?

565
34:41.726 --> 34:44.479
Growing them in an open field seems like a lot of unnecessary trial and error.

566
34:44.562 --> 34:45.897
It seems a bit impractical.

567
34:47.774 --> 34:49.150
[Karin, in English] You're right.

568
34:49.234 --> 34:52.487
In a greenhouse, the environment is controlled.

569
34:52.570 --> 34:55.782
-It would make my life a lot easier. -[in Korean] Right.

570
34:58.243 --> 34:59.619
So what if…

571
35:01.454 --> 35:02.455
And that's a huge "if."

572
35:02.539 --> 35:04.457
What if someone were to buy that land for a lot of money?

573
35:04.541 --> 35:06.084
Wouldn't it make more sense to just sell it off,

574
35:06.167 --> 35:08.420
move your crops, and upgrade to a big greenhouse?

575
35:08.503 --> 35:10.046
It'd be way more convenient.

576
35:13.550 --> 35:15.218
[in English] That's true in theory.

577
35:15.719 --> 35:18.179
Fruit grows in rhythm with every single season,

578
35:19.139 --> 35:21.391
allowing nature's flavor to absorb.

579
35:22.475 --> 35:24.394
[♪ gentle music playing]

580
35:26.396 --> 35:27.480
[chuckles]

581
35:27.981 --> 35:30.358
I learned that from my grandfather.

582
35:30.442 --> 35:34.487
Which is why I decided to grow my strawberries outside instead.

583
35:36.906 --> 35:40.326
You could say that it's a personal experiment.

584
35:41.244 --> 35:43.621
Does it really make a difference or not?

585
35:43.705 --> 35:47.625
Does the power of mother nature affect how delicious they can be?

586
35:51.004 --> 35:52.005
[chuckles]

587
35:53.298 --> 35:56.092
Anyway, I noticed your effort today.

588
35:56.176 --> 35:58.344
Although you were barely any help.

589
35:59.763 --> 36:01.848
[in Korean] Is that a compliment or an insult?

590
36:03.475 --> 36:06.352
[in English] In appreciation, you can come over for dinner.

591
36:07.061 --> 36:08.104
You earned it.

592
36:08.188 --> 36:09.731
[chuckles]

593
36:17.197 --> 36:18.323
[in Korean] Let's go!

594
36:18.406 --> 36:20.700
[in English] What? No, wait! [laughs]

595
36:28.208 --> 36:31.878
[music ends]

596
36:46.893 --> 36:47.894
Good evening.

597
36:48.645 --> 36:49.938
Ah.

598
36:50.021 --> 36:53.107
Hi. Good evening. Have a seat.

599
36:54.234 --> 36:55.235
Ah.

600
36:55.735 --> 36:56.736
-Ah. -[Karin] Mmm.

601
36:56.820 --> 36:59.030
[chuckles] Please, wait a minute.

602
37:01.991 --> 37:03.827
[♪ intriguing music playing]

603
37:19.133 --> 37:20.510
CERTIFICATE OF RECOGNITION

604
37:23.930 --> 37:24.931
[chuckles]

605
37:30.311 --> 37:31.312
[in Korean] Huh?

606
37:32.772 --> 37:33.898
Wow.

607
37:34.816 --> 37:37.110
This guy's from my favorite game when I was little.

608
37:37.193 --> 37:38.528
What are the chances?

609
37:41.072 --> 37:42.073
[in English] Okay.

610
37:43.449 --> 37:45.034
Come sit. It's ready.

611
37:45.118 --> 37:46.286
Ah.

612
37:49.122 --> 37:50.123
Here you are.

613
37:51.666 --> 37:52.667
[music ends]

614
37:52.750 --> 37:53.751
Okay.

615
37:56.045 --> 37:59.549
I know when it's better to use the carrot or the stick.

616
38:06.139 --> 38:08.975
[in Korean] What are you going to make me do tomorrow?

617
38:11.269 --> 38:12.812
-[in English] You're not hungry? -[in Korean] No, no.

618
38:13.354 --> 38:15.106
[in English] Uh. Thank you for the meal.

619
38:16.232 --> 38:17.567
Time to eat.

620
38:19.652 --> 38:21.487
Oh! I forgot something.

621
38:21.571 --> 38:22.780
Huh?

622
38:27.619 --> 38:29.662
You should know what this is.

623
38:30.538 --> 38:32.957
Korean-style pickled perilla leaves.

624
38:34.375 --> 38:35.585
Oh?

625
38:35.668 --> 38:38.254
[in Korean] Wait, this is a Korean side dish. How do you know it?

626
38:38.338 --> 38:39.589
[chuckles]

627
38:39.672 --> 38:42.967
[in English] When I was little, a Korean man used to board with us.

628
38:43.051 --> 38:44.636
I learned the recipe from him.

629
38:45.720 --> 38:46.721
Oh.

630
38:47.347 --> 38:52.727
The red pepper is for "love," and the daikon radish is for "health."

631
38:56.189 --> 38:59.150
So you're getting both love and health.

632
39:01.069 --> 39:02.320
[♪ sad, emotional music playing]

633
39:08.576 --> 39:09.661
[in Korean] There.

634
39:10.370 --> 39:11.371
Hmm?

635
39:11.955 --> 39:14.207
This again? I'm so sick of it.

636
39:14.874 --> 39:16.793
It's your dad's favorite.

637
39:16.876 --> 39:19.253
He hasn't been home in a while, so stop complaining and eat.

638
39:19.337 --> 39:23.216
Son, this dish here is full of love and health.

639
39:23.716 --> 39:24.717
Take a look.

640
39:25.468 --> 39:26.761
Here's love.

641
39:28.137 --> 39:29.555
And here's health.

642
39:31.140 --> 39:32.642
And you wrap it up…

643
39:35.937 --> 39:37.188
Just try it.

644
39:38.439 --> 39:41.025
-For you. -Me? [chuckles]

645
39:41.109 --> 39:42.568
Your health matters the most.

646
39:43.069 --> 39:44.654
I can't say no to that.

647
39:48.866 --> 39:51.077
[Karin, in English] That man was so kind to us.

648
39:52.120 --> 39:55.123
He took extra care of my grandpa after he collapsed.

649
39:55.206 --> 39:58.584
And he taught me a lot about growing strawberries.

650
40:01.087 --> 40:06.092
Mr. Gyeongsu was a very wonderful man, but you're the complete opposite.

651
40:10.096 --> 40:11.264
Ah…

652
40:12.807 --> 40:15.268
[in Korean] I'm actually not feeling so great. Sorry.

653
40:21.691 --> 40:23.651
[footsteps departing]

654
40:23.735 --> 40:24.736
[music ends]

655
40:35.830 --> 40:38.416
[♪ somber music playing]

656
40:42.837 --> 40:44.756
What on earth was he doing here?

657
40:45.506 --> 40:47.467
INTERNAL USE

658
40:47.550 --> 40:50.595
[thunder rumbling]

659
40:51.429 --> 40:54.432
[sirens wailing in distance]

660
40:56.684 --> 40:57.852
[coughing]

661
41:19.415 --> 41:23.419
[siren blaring]

662
41:33.596 --> 41:36.516
-[panting echoing] -[high-pitched ringing]

663
41:37.892 --> 41:38.893
[Yubin] Mom.

664
41:52.323 --> 41:53.699
[panting]

665
42:00.748 --> 42:01.749
[sobbing] Mom.

666
42:02.917 --> 42:04.585
Mom!

667
43:29.503 --> 43:31.297
[in Korean] Are you okay?

668
43:34.383 --> 43:39.597
[♪ upbeat music playing]

669
44:09.710 --> 44:11.963
MERRY BERRY LOVE

670
44:12.046 --> 44:13.130
NEXT EPISODE

671
44:13.214 --> 44:15.800
[Karin, in English] We are not sleeping in the same space.

672
44:15.883 --> 44:18.010
[Yubin] I love rules. I really do.

673
44:18.094 --> 44:20.263
-[in Korean] Rock, paper, scissors! -[both scream]

674
44:20.346 --> 44:22.014
[Karin, in English] Why is my heart pounding?
